d 'THRESHKIT': module to estimate hreshold models for cross-section and time series
d
d    threshkit brings the threshold-model family into a single
d package: abrupt (jump) thresholds, continuous kinks, smooth
d transitions, asymmetric adjustment and bands of inaction,
d together with the multivariate counterparts -- threshold VAR,
d threshold VECM and vector smooth transition VAR. It covers the
d three stages a threshold analysis actually goes through. First,
d whether there is a threshold at all. The threshold is not
d identified under the null, so the linearity and
d threshold-existence tests carry the bootstrap p-values that
d requires, with Davies' analytic bound available as a cheap
d alternative (Hansen 1996, 2000; Davies 1987). Second, estimation
d and inference. Least-squares, quantile, instrumental- variable
d and endogenous-threshold estimators, with
d inverted-likelihood-ratio confidence sets for the threshold
d rather than a standard error its limit distribution does not
d support, and the conservative intervals of Donayre, Eo and Morley
d (2018) alongside. Third, post-estimation. Regime diagnostics
d against the regime-split design, generalised impulse responses
d (Koop, Pesaran and Potter 1996), the deterministic skeleton with
d its limit cycles, forecasting, and publication-ready tables and
d graphs. 
d
d KW: threshold models
d KW: smooth transitions
d KW: asymmetric adjuistment
d
d Requires: Stata version 15
d
d Distribution-Date: 20261009
d
d Author:   Merwan Roudane, NA
d Support: email  merwanroudane920@@gmail.com
d
